Goddamn this game is awesome. This was my first genocideless
ascension.. really the first game i had to tangle with L's, mindflayers
or ;. Fun factor increased by 400% - never goin back.

After I ascended a wizard, i tried my hand at archeologists and
healers...
alternating with each death. It took me a long ass time to get a healer
through both the mines and soko... constant weapon problems. Seemed
i couldn't get either a unicorn horn or a crysknife. One game i got
Mojo, but that ended with a potion of paralysis and some elf lords.

With Bill, i got an elven dagger in a shop and sting'd it pretty early
on..
it served me throughout the mines, until my dog killed a unicorn for
me.
First time i'd used unicorn horn as a weapon... it worked very well-
used it until i got the staff.

My repeated failures w/ wizards helped me out and netted me a
CoMR and a buncha magic markers. The minetown altar was coaligned
so it was pretty super, and a hardware store had a magic lamp.

I got to the castle without finding any ?oGeno, and had more or less
completed my ascension kit (YDSM, CoMR, "oR (from bones), BoH
(from soko), =oSD <3, =oConflict, waterwalking boots, a spell of
jumping,
gauntlets of dex... pretty much everything but speedboots and a
=oLevitation), and i'd already run into a few liches and mindflayers
and
managed to handle them well, so i figured i'd go for
wishless/genocideless.

Wishless held out until a soldier wacked me w/ a cockatrice corpse
early on
in Gehennom. Zapped myself w/ stone2flesh and that killed my rings,
touchstone, luckstone, and a bunch of wands. Shortly after, an archlich
found me and proceeded to kick my ass and i began to starve. Survived
by the skin of my teeth, and went ahead and wished for another =oSD.
Since i had already broken conduct, i went ahead and wished for some
magic markers, an oilskin cloak and used the GDS i'd stashed away
earlier.

Cyclops didn't pose too much of a problem. He knocked me down
from lvl 14 to 9, but my HP never hit critical, tho i had to cast
extra healing a few times. Just kept wackin' him with a +7 unicorn
horn till he went down.

Charmed a buncha purple worms in gehennom... i never realized
their intense utility. Whenever a mindflayer got remotely close
i just whistled them in and they'd burp away. Lost 'em all in
Rodney's tower tho, and didn't bother to get anymore once
the wiz was on my ass.

Yeenoghu got summoned chez Jubilex.. not sure how.. i think
it was from a magic trap- is that possible? Beat him down with
the staff.

I must take an aside to say that ole Thom Fine was right on the money
about the Staff of Aes. Once i got it i only switched to the saber
once-
for the shades... tho i did take out Orcus with a cockatrice corpse.
The staff kicked absolute ass- had no problem whatsoever w/ the
named demons or elementals, or even Rodney! My /oD ran outta
charges in the Sanctum, and i just beat him down man to man
every time after (4 or 5 times).

After rodney, pretty much kept conflict on the rest of the way.
In the sanctum, an Elvenking read a ?oCM, and i got pinned
with a mindflayer which proceeded to stupify me. Forgot a lotta
the dungeon and a lotta items, oh well.

The planes weren't much trouble, though on Air an archon
repeatedly summoned a buncha nasties right around the portal,
and i had trouble finding it again.

In Astral, kept conflict on... i think it was much better that way.
Went left first (had a helm of opposite alignment handy, but didn't end

up needing it). Killed pestilence hand-to-hand, and teleported everyone
out of the way until i reached the good ole altar of Hermes.

Most satisfying game i've yet played. I spose next i'll go for a rogue
or ranger... or maybe a wishless valk... It seems that once you
hit -42 AC and max out your stats, race and class really don't matter
too much.

NHIAWOL,
Jonker

